       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 400 mg daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum of 200 mg/day. Higher doses carry a greater risk of serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, GI effects, and bleeding, and I don't see a rationale for going above the maximum. Your patient's weight, kidney function, and liver function don't change that ceiling.\n\nCould you check which of these applies?\n\n1. **Typo or unit error.** If you meant 40 mg or 200 mg, I can enter that right away. Typical dosing is 50 mg daily to start, titrated up to 200 mg.\n2. **Intentional supratherapeutic dose.** If you do mean 400 mg, for example on a specialist's recommendation, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting the rationale. Pharmacy will probably want to verify it.\n\nWhich would you like?"
